   129	The normative model was then applied to the testing dataset. Between-network FC was predicted in the testing dataset ( ̂ FCi ). Deviation scores (z) were then calculated by subtracting predicted betweennetwork FC from actual between-network FC, and dividing the difference by the training dataset standard deviation (population standard deviation). These z scores reflect the individual degree of betweennetwork FC atypicality from a typically developing population mean.
